---
import SketchLayout from '../../layouts/SketchLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/sketch-d.css';
---

<SketchLayout title="Sketch D — Local Loop · Hozz" letter="D" name="Local Loop">
  <main>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <header class="masthead">
        <a class="wordmark" href="#hero-title" aria-label="Hozz, back to top">HOZZ</a>
        <p class="status"><span aria-hidden="true"></span> Early alpha · open source</p>
      </header>

      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="kicker">Your health data, as local context</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">Let your assistant read your health history.<br /><em>Without giving it away.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Hozz keeps what your iPhone sends in a SQLite file on your Mac, then exposes it through an
          enforced read-only MCP server. Your assistant comes to the data—not the other way around.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="local-loop" aria-label="Diagram: an AI assistant reads health data locally through Hozz's read-only MCP server">
        <svg class="loop-line" viewBox="0 0 1200 380" role="img" aria-labelledby="loop-title loop-desc">
          <title id="loop-title">The Hozz local data loop</title>
          <desc id="loop-desc">Health data stays in a SQLite file on your Mac. An assistant can request read-only access through four MCP tools.</desc>
          <path class="rail rail-shadow" d="M108 190 C260 16 410 16 552 190 S850 364 1092 190" />
          <path class="rail rail-active" d="M108 190 C260 16 410 16 552 190 S850 364 1092 190" />
        </svg>

        <article class="node node-data">
          <div class="node-index">LOCAL / 01</div>
          <h2>Your Mac</h2>
          <p class="file">hozz-received.sqlite</p>
          <p class="node-note">The source file stays here.</p>
        </article>

        <div class="gate">
          <p class="gate-label">READ ONLY</p>
          <div class="gate-mark" aria-hidden="true">
            <span></span><span></span><span></span>
          </div>
          <p class="gate-protocol">MCP · stdio</p>
        </div>

        <article class="node node-assistant">
          <div class="node-index">LOCAL / 02</div>
          <h2>Your assistant</h2>
          <p class="node-note">Reads only what you ask it to.</p>
        </article>

        <ul class="tools" aria-label="The four read-only tools">
          <li>list_health_types</li>
          <li>summarise_health_data</li>
          <li>aggregate_health_data</li>
          <li>list_health_samples</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-foot">
        <p class="proof"><strong>Cannot change. Cannot delete.</strong> Read-only is enforced in the server, not promised in copy.</p>
        <a class="inspect-link" href="#inspect">Inspect the connection <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="inspect" id="inspect" aria-labelledby="inspect-title">
      <div class="inspect-copy">
        <p class="kicker">The whole connection</p>
        <h2 id="inspect-title">A small config.<br />No hosted relay.</h2>
        <p>
          The Assistant tab in the Mac app generates this. Paste it into an MCP-compatible assistant
          to point the assistant at the Hozz server and your local data directory.
        </p>
        <dl class="facts">
          <div><dt>Protocol</dt><dd>JSON-RPC 2.0 · 2024-11-05</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Server</dt><dd>hozz · 1.0.0</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Licence</dt><dd>GPL-3.0 + App Store exception</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>

      <figure class="config-card">
        <figcaption><span>assistant-config.json</span><span>generated locally</span></figcaption>
        <pre><code><span class="punct">&lbrace;</span>
  <span class="key">"mcpServers"</span>: <span class="punct">&lbrace;</span>
    <span class="key">"hozz"</span>: <span class="punct">&lbrace;</span>
      <span class="key">"command"</span>:
        <span class="string">"/Applications/Hozz.app/Contents/MacOS/hozz-mcp"</span>,
      <span class="key">"args"</span>: <span class="punct">[</span>
        <span class="string">"--data-dir"</span>,
        <span class="string">"/Users/you/Library/.../Hozz/Received"</span>
      <span class="punct">]</span>
    <span class="punct">&rbrace;</span>
  <span class="punct">&rbrace;</span>
<span class="punct">&rbrace;</span></code></pre>
      </figure>

      <aside class="caveat">
        <p class="caveat-label">One honest boundary</p>
        <p>
          If you connect Hozz to a cloud-hosted assistant, that assistant may upload whatever it reads.
          That is the assistant’s behaviour, not Hozz’s.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </section>
  </main>
</SketchLayout>
